\label{lem:weakly-unramified-inclusion}
Let \(M_0\in\operatorname{Perv}_{\mathrm{int}}^{\mathrm{ari}}(\mathbb{G}_m^d/k)\) be arithmetically semisimple, let
\(M=M_{0,\bar k}\), and let \(L=M\oplus M^\vee\).  Then \(X_w(L)\subseteq X(M_0)\).

\label{lem:constant-tensor}
Let \(f\colon X\to Y\) be any morphism of schemes and let \(V\) be a finite-dimensional
\(\ol\mathbb{Q}_{\ell}\)-vector space.  For \(Z=X,Y\), let \(V_Z\) be the constant sheaf on
\(Z_{\mathrm{pro\acute et}}\) associated with \(V\).  The tensor products below are derived tensor
products of \(\ol\mathbb{Q}_{\ell}\)-sheaves.  For \(K\in D(X_{\mathrm{pro\acute et}},\ol\mathbb{Q}_{\ell})\), the natural morphism
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:constant-tensor}
        \theta_{K,V}\colon
        Rf_*K\otimes_{\ol\mathbb{Q}_{\ell}}V_Y
        \longrightarrow
        Rf_*(K\otimes_{\ol\mathbb{Q}_{\ell}}V_X)
\end{equation}
is an isomorphism, naturally in \(K\) and in \(V\).
